. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
. *** AS SPECIFIED IN THE PAP: Match treatment variables from years 2001, 2006,
>  2011, 2016 (pld0026) with the outcomes measured in 2005, 2009, 2014, 2019
. *** Note that the data generation of the treatment variable (d_daughter) and 
> the recoding of marital status (pgfamstd -> married) happens within each of t
> he following code chunks.
. *** Note: We use sumkids and daughter instead of pld0025 and bgp15307a (which
>  we mentioned in our PAP), since these variables did not contain the desired 
> information for all necessary years
. *** Recode marital status: coded as one if married (1); married, but separate
> d (2); husband/wife abroad (6); civil union living together or apart (7 and 8
> ); coded as zero if single(3); divorced(4); widowed(5)
. 
. *** SOMEWHAT MEANINGFUL CHANGE TO WHAT WE SPECIFIED IN THE PAP: DUE TO A MISU
> NDERSTANDING OF THE AVAILABILITY OF THE 
. *** GENDER OF CHILDREN VARIABLES, WE CAME UP WITH THE TREATMENT /LAGGED OUTCO
> MES DESIGN DESCRIBED ABOVE
. *** WE NOW SEE THAT WE CAN ACTUALLY USE THE INFORMATION ON THE TREATMENT VARI
> ABLE FROM THE SAME YEAR AS FOR THE OUTCOME VARIABLES
. *** WE HAVE KEPT THE CODE FOR THE PAP BELOW IN COMMENTS, BUT USE THE SLIGHTLY
>  ADAPTED CODE WITHOUT THE LAGGED OUTCOMES FOR THE ANALYSIS
. *** BECAUSE IT AVOIDS POTENTIAL ISSUES DUE TO THE LAG BETWEEN TREATMENT AND O
> UTCOME MEASUREMENT THAT COULD BIAS OUR ESTIMATES
. 
. *preserve
. *       keep if syear==2001
. *       keep if sumkids==1
. *       gen d_daughter=1 if kidsex01==2
. *       replace d_daughter = 0 if d_daughter==.
. *       count
. *       keep if pgfamstd >=0
. *       gen married = 0 if pgfamstd==3|pgfamstd==4|pgfamstd==5
. *       replace married = 1 if married==.
. *       keep pid syear d_daughter gebjahr sex pgisced97 pgemplst married
